description:
Currently Kerberos errors are presented as a stack trace to the user looking something like:

{noformat}
GSSError: (('Unspecified GSS failure.  Minor code may provide more information', 851968), ('No Kerberos credentials available', -1765328243))
401 Client Error: Authorization Required
{noformat}

(And similar for expired tickets). It would be helpful to catch these and display more useful information, such as a suggestion to run {{kinit}}.

summary_description_acceptance:
Improve client error messages for Kerberos errors $end$ Currently Kerberos errors are presented as a stack trace to the user looking something like:

{noformat}
GSSError: (('Unspecified GSS failure.  Minor code may provide more information', 851968), ('No Kerberos credentials available', -1765328243))
401 Client Error: Authorization Required
{noformat}

(And similar for expired tickets). It would be helpful to catch these and display more useful information, such as a suggestion to run {{kinit}}. $acceptance criteria:$

original_description_sprint:
Currently Kerberos errors are presented as a stack trace to the user looking something like:

{noformat}
GSSError: (('Unspecified GSS failure.  Minor code may provide more information', 851968), ('No Kerberos credentials available', -1765328243))
401 Client Error: Authorization Required
{noformat}

(And similar for expired tickets). It would be helpful to catch these and display more useful information, such as a suggestion to run {{kinit}}.

original_summary_description_acceptance_:
Improve client error messages for Kerberos errors $end$ Currently Kerberos errors are presented as a stack trace to the user looking something like:

