description:
As far as I can tell, current practice is to quote code excerpts and object names with backticks when writing comments. For example:

{code}
// You know, `sadPanda` seems extra sad lately.
std::string sadPanda;
sadPanda = "   :'(   ";
{code}

However, I don't see this documented in our C++ style guide at all. It should be added.

summary_description_acceptance:
Backticks are not mentioned in Mesos C++ Style Guide $end$ As far as I can tell, current practice is to quote code excerpts and object names with backticks when writing comments. For example:

